Client B disconnects

Suppose Client A keeps the connection open using Keep-Alive but does not send another request for 20 seconds.

During those 20 seconds:

The server is still inside handle_client(Client A).
Client B cannot be accepted or processed.
Every other client must wait.

Although the CPU may be idle waiting for network data, the server cannot serve other clients because only one thread is executing.

How do Threads solve this?

Instead of handling every client in the main thread, we create a separate thread for each client connection.

Main Thread

↓

accept(Client A)

↓

Thread 1

↓

handle_client(Client A)

Immediately after creating Thread 1, the main thread becomes free again.

Main Thread

↓

accept(Client B)

↓

Thread 2

↓

handle_client(Client B)

Now multiple client connections can be handled simultaneously.

Each thread waits only for its own client.

If Client A is idle, Thread 1 waits for Client A while Thread 2 continues serving Client B.

